{
  "about": "Popular books for United States libraries, groups interleaved: classic (school reading), fiction (recent), nonfiction, children, ya (young adult) and spanish. The first forty, in order of broad public-library appeal, were chosen on 23 November 2026 and the next forty added on 24 November 2026, all from a 120-title candidate pool researched on 23 November: distinctive titles of two or more words; single-word or generic titles (The Women, The Giver, Animal Farm, Into the Wild), a title whose words repeat (Tomorrow, and Tomorrow, and Tomorrow), 1984 / Nineteen Eighty-Four, the Sorcerer's / Philosopher's Stone pair and Spanish editions of books already here are left out (the app's 80% title-word matcher would find other books for them). Uses: the app's first-open suggestions for a US library (the first twenty, one book per author; client/src/v2/suggestions/seed.ts), so new books go at the end; and the US library pages, ten books each from the whole list, a stable mix chosen by the library's ID (tools/seo/check-pages.mjs bookMix: a seeded shuffle, at least one book of each group, at most three of one group, one per author). Nothing here says a library has a book. bookKey (the Open Library work), isbn (one ISBN-13 of the work) and coverId (the work's cover) come from openlibrary.org search: `node tools/seo/library-shelves.mjs pool --file shared/us-book-pool.json --covers` (it keeps an ISBN already given; Braiding Sweetgrass has the Milkweed Editions English paperback, set by hand on 23 November 2026, because the search gave a Spanish edition's ISBN). updatedOn is the date this list last changed; a page's sitemap date follows its own ten books (shared/seo-us-libraries.json mix).",
